/* book Worked example 2: Q: A lever of rectangular section 15 mm wide and 45 mm deep is pushed by a 1.2 kN force at 300 mm from its pivot. The pivot pin is 20 mm in diameter and carries 30 kN in double shear. Find the bending stress in the lever at the pivot, the maximum transverse shear stress in the lever and the shear stress in the pin.
   1. Bending moment at the pivot: M = 1200 × 300 = 360,000 N·mm.
   2. Z = bh²/6 = 15 × 45²/6 = 5062.5 mm³. Bending stress σb = 360,000/5062.5 = 71.1 MPa.
   3. Transverse shear in the lever: V = 1200 N, A = 15 × 45 = 675 mm², τmax = 1.5 × 1200/675 = 2.67 MPa, about 4 % of the bending stress.
   4. Pin in double shear: A = 2 × π × 20²/4 = 628.3 mm²; τ = 30,000/628.3 = 47.7 MPa.
   Answer: Lever: σb = 71.1 MPa, transverse shear 2.67 MPa (negligible). Pin: τ = 47.7 MPa. */
